FILE: vUX-marquee.js
FEATURE: marquee-module
DATE: 2026-10-11
PRIOR STATE: as left by feature 'message-box-module' (uncommitted at the time)

REASON
NEW FILE. The Marquee module: an endless, seamless scrolling strip. Requested so the
technology strip on vilshub.com (Apps/vilshub.com), written there by hand with a doubled
list and a -50% CSS loop, becomes a reusable vUX component.

Design points worth recording:

  - Items written once. initialize() moves the container's element children into a
    track ($$.ce("div", {class:"vMarqueeTrack"})) and appends clone sets until the track
    covers the container width plus one set. A hand-doubled list breaks on screens wider
    than one copy; this does not.

  - Measured loop. The distance per loop is clones[0].offsetLeft - items[0].offsetLeft,
    so it includes config.gap and any item margins, and the end frame matches the start.

  - Web Animations API (track.animate) rather than a keyframes rule in marquee.css, so
    the strip is right before the stylesheet arrives (it is linked about 300ms after
    load). The structural styles the measurement depends on are inline for the same
    reason. Speed, direction, gap and reduced-motion changes restart the animation at
    the same progress, so a running strip never jumps; direction mirrors the progress.

  - ResizeObserver on the container and the track rebuilds when the container width or
    the set width changes (fonts arriving, edits). A rebuild that only adds clones does
    not change either value, so it does not trigger itself.

  - Clones: aria-hidden, ids stripped, tabindex="-1" on anything focusable. Not inert:
    inert also blocks clicks, and about half the visible items are clones. Found while
    writing the example's linked-cards section.

  - pauseOnHover covers keyboard focus too (focusin/focusout), so a link can be read
    before it scrolls away.

  - destroy() puts the items back in order, removes track and clones, and restores the
    container's own classes and inline styles (saved per property on first write).

MANUAL OPERATION REPORTED TO THE USER
  reducedMotion(): the same matchMedia check MessageBox has locally (potential utility #2).
  Added Marquee to that row in .claude/projects/vUX/potentialUtilities.md.

